{"id":"mahabharata-7-147","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":147,"title":"सप्तचत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 147 · Night: the Kauravas rally","summary":{"en":"Seeing his army routed, Duryodhana in rage attacks the Pandava army, and Drona is struck by Bhima and Dhrishtadyumna. The Kauravas rally around Drona and the dark night grows deeper.","kn":"ತನ್ನ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಓಡುವುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಕೋಪದಿಂದ ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯದ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಮ, ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನರು ದ್ರೋಣನನ್ನು ಹೊಡೆಯುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಕೌರವರು ದ್ರೋಣನ ಸುತ್ತ ಒಗ್ಗೂಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ರಾತ್ರಿ ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ಗಾಢವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"अपनी सेना को भागते देख दुर्योधन क्रोध से पाण्डव सेना पर टूटता है, और द्रोण पर भीम तथा धृष्टद्युम्न प्रहार करते हैं। कौरव द्रोण के चारों ओर संगठित होते हैं और रात और गहरी हो जाती है।","te":"తన సేన పారిపోవడం చూసి దుర్యోధనుడు కోపంతో పాండవసేనపై దూకుతాడు; భీముడు, ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుడు ద్రోణుని కొడతారు. కౌరవులు ద్రోణుని చుట్టూ చేరతారు; రాత్రి మరింత గాఢమవుతుంది.","ta":"தன் படை தோற்றோடுவதைக் கண்ட துரியோதனன் சினத்துடன் பாண்டவப் படையைத் தாக்க, பீமனும் த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னனும் த்ரோணரைத் தாக்குகின்றனர். கௌரவர் த்ரோணரைச் சுற்றித் திரள, இரவு மேலும் ஆழ்கிறது.","ml":"തന്റെ സേന തകർന്നതു കണ്ട് കോപത്തോടെ ദുര്യോധനൻ പാണ്ഡവ സേനയെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; ഭീമനും ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നനും ദ്രോണരെ പ്രഹരിക്കുന്നു. കൗരവർ ദ്രോണരെ ചുറ്റി ഒന്നിക്കുന്നു; ഇരുണ്ട രാത്രി കൂടുതൽ ആഴമേറുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.147; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विद्रुतं स्वबलं दृष्ट्वा वध्यमानं महात्मभिः ।\nक्रोधेन महताविष्टः पुत्रस्तव विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his own force in flight and being cut down by the great-souled enemies, your son, O lord of the people, was filled with great anger."}},{"n":2,"text":"अभ्येत्य सहसा कर्णं द्रोणं च जयतां वरम् ।\nअमर्षवशमापन्नो वाक्यज्ञो वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suddenly coming to Karna and Drona, the best of victors, he spoke these words, overcome with indignation, skilled in speech."}},{"n":3,"text":"भवद्भ्यामिह संग्रामो क्रुद्धाभ्यां संप्रवर्तितः ।\nआहवे निहतं दृष्ट्वा सैन्धवं सव्यसाचिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said: \"You two began this war here in anger, after seeing the Sindhu king killed in battle by Savyasachin."}},{"n":4,"text":"निहन्यमानां पाण्डूनां बलेन मम वाहिनीम् ।\nभूत्वा तद्विजये शक्तावशक्ताविव पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet, being able to win it, you look on as if powerless while my army is slaughtered by the Pandavas' force."}},{"n":5,"text":"यद्यहं भवतोस्त्याज्यो न वाच्योऽस्मि तदैव हि ।\nआवां पाण्डुसुतान्संख्ये जेष्याव इति मानदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I was to be abandoned by you, you should have told me then, honored ones, that you would never claim to conquer the sons of Pandu in battle."}},{"n":6,"text":"तदैवाहं वचः श्रुत्वा भवद्भ्यामनुसंमतम् ।\nकृतवान्पाण्डवैः सार्धं वैरं योधविनाशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, hearing your agreement, I made this enmity with the Pandavas, which destroys warriors."}},{"n":7,"text":"यदि नाहं परित्याज्यो भवद्भ्यां पुरुषर्षभौ ।\nयुध्येतामनुरूपेण विक्रमेण सुविक्रमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I am not to be abandoned by you two, bulls among men, then fight, mighty ones, with valor to match.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"वाक्प्रतोदेन तौ वीरौ प्रणुन्नौ तनयेन ते ।\nप्रावर्तयेतां तौ युद्धं घट्टिताविव पन्नगौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Goaded by your son's whip of words, those two heroes began the battle, like two snakes that have been struck."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततस्तौ रथिनां श्रेष्ठौ सर्वलोकधनुर्धरौ ।\nशैनेयप्रमुखान्पार्थानभिदुद्रुवतू रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those best of charioteers, archers famed in all the world, rushed in the battle at the Parthas led by Shaineya."}},{"n":10,"text":"तथैव सहिताः पार्थाः स्वेन सैन्येन संवृताः ।\nअभ्यवर्तन्त तौ वीरौ नर्दमानौ मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And likewise the Parthas, together and surrounded by their own army, advanced against those two heroes, who were roaring again and again."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथ द्रोणो महेष्वासो दशभिः शिनिपुंगवम् ।\nअविध्यत्त्वरितं क्रुद्धः सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona, the great archer, best of all weapon-bearers, angrily and quickly pierced the bull of the Shinis (Satyaki) with ten arrows."}},{"n":12,"text":"कर्णश्च दशभिर्बाणैः पुत्रश्च तव सप्तभिः ।\nदशभिर्वृषसेनश्च सौबलश्चापि सप्तभिः ।\nएते कौरव संक्रन्दे शैनेयं पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna with ten arrows, your son with seven, Vrishasena with ten, and Shakuni with seven: these, O Kaurava, surrounded Shaineya in that uproar."}},{"n":13,"text":"दृष्ट्वा च समरे द्रोणं निघ्नन्तं पाण्डवीं चमूम् ।\nविव्यधुः सोमकास्तूर्णं समन्ताच्छरवृष्टिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Drona killing the Pandava army in the battle, the Somakas quickly struck him from all sides with showers of arrows."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततो द्रोणोऽहरत्प्राणान्क्षत्रियाणां विशां पते ।\nरश्मिभिर्भास्करो राजंस्तमसामिव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona took the lives of the kshatriyas, O lord of the people, as the sun with his rays takes darkness, Bharata."}},{"n":15,"text":"द्रोणेन वध्यमानानां पाञ्चालानां विशां पते ।\nशुश्रुवे तुमुलः शब्दः क्रोशतामितरेतरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Panchalas were being killed by Drona, a tumultuous sound was heard, of them calling to one another."}},{"n":16,"text":"पुत्रानन्ये पितॄनन्ये भ्रातॄनन्ये च मातुलान् ।\nभागिनेयान्वयस्यांश्च तथा संबन्धिबान्धवान् ।\nउत्सृज्योत्सृज्य गच्छन्ति त्वरिता जीवितेप्सवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some abandoned their sons, some their fathers, brothers, uncles, nephews, friends, in-laws and kinsmen, and went off in haste, wanting to save their lives."}},{"n":17,"text":"अपरे मोहिता मोहात्तमेवाभिमुखा ययुः ।\nपाण्डवानां रणे योधाः परलोकं तथापरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, bewildered, went straight toward him in their confusion; those warriors of the Pandavas went to the other world."}},{"n":18,"text":"सा तथा पाण्डवी सेना वध्यमाना महात्मभिः ।\nनिशि संप्राद्रवद्राजन्नुत्सृज्योल्काः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So that Pandava army, being struck down by the great-souled warriors, fled in the night, O king, throwing away thousands of torches."}},{"n":19,"text":"पश्यतो भीमसेनस्य विजयस्याच्युतस्य च ।\nयमयोर्धर्मपुत्रस्य पार्षतस्य च पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Bhimasena, Vijaya (Arjuna) and Achyuta (Krishna), the twins, Dharma's son and Prishata's son looked on,"}},{"n":20,"text":"तमसा संवृते लोके न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ।\nकौरवाणां प्रकाशेन दृश्यन्ते तु द्रुताः परे ॥","meaning":{"en":"with the world wrapped in darkness nothing could be known; only by the Kauravas' light could the fleeing enemy be seen."}},{"n":21,"text":"द्रवमाणं तु तत्सैन्यं द्रोणकर्णौ महारथौ ।\nजघ्नतुः पृष्ठतो राजन्किरन्तौ सायकान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that army fled, the two great warriors Drona and Karna struck it from behind, O king, scattering many arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"पाञ्चालेषु प्रभग्नेषु दीर्यमाणेषु सर्वशः ।\nजनार्दनो दीनमनाः प्रत्यभाषत फल्गुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the Panchalas were broken and torn on every side, Janardana, sad at heart, said to Phalguna:"}},{"n":23,"text":"द्रोणकर्णौ महेष्वासावेतौ पार्षतसात्यकी ।\nपाञ्चालांश्चैव सहितौ जघ्नतुः सायकैर्भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Drona and Karna, the two great archers, and Prishata's son with Satyaki together have been smashing the Panchalas hard with arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"एतयोः शरवर्षेण प्रभग्ना नो महारथाः ।\nवार्यमाणापि कौन्तेय पृतना नावतिष्ठते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our great warriors have been broken by the arrow-rain of these two, and though held back, Kunti's son, the army will not stand."}},{"n":25,"text":"एतावावां सर्वसैन्यैर्व्यूढैः सम्यगुदायुधैः ।\nद्रोणं च सूतपुत्रं च प्रयतावः प्रबाधितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let us two make an effort to hinder Drona and the charioteer's son, with all our armies in array and weapons raised."}},{"n":26,"text":"एतौ हि बलिनौ शूरौ कृतास्त्रौ जितकाशिनौ ।\nउपेक्षितौ बलं क्रुद्धौ नाशयेतां निशामिमाम् ।\nएष भीमोऽभियात्युग्रः पुनरावर्त्य वाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two are strong, brave, skilled in weapons and victorious; if neglected in their anger they will destroy our force this night. And here Bhima is coming fiercely, having turned the army around.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"वृकोदरं तथायान्तं दृष्ट्वा तत्र जनार्दनः ।\nपुनरेवाब्रवीद्राजन्हर्षयन्निव पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Vrikodara come there, Janardana spoke again to the Pandava, as if to cheer him."}},{"n":28,"text":"एष भीमो रणश्लाघी वृतः सोमकपाण्डवैः ।\nरुषितोऽभ्येति वेगेन द्रोणकर्णौ महाबलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is Bhima, who delights in battle, surrounded by Somakas and Pandavas, coming angrily and swiftly at the mighty Drona and Karna."}},{"n":29,"text":"एतेन सहितो युध्य पाञ्चालैश्च महारथैः ।\nआश्वासनार्थं सर्वेषां सैन्यानां पाण्डुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fight together with him and the great-warrior Panchalas, joy of Pandu, to reassure all the armies.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"ततस्तौ पुरुषव्याघ्रावुभौ माधवपाण्डवौ ।\nद्रोणकर्णौ समासाद्य धिष्ठितौ रणमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those two tigers among men, the Madhava and the Pandava, reaching Drona and Karna, took their stand at the head of the battle."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततस्तत्पुनरावृत्तं युधिष्ठिरबलं महत् ।\nततो द्रोणश्च कर्णश्च परान्ममृदतुर्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira's great force rallied; and then Drona and Karna crushed the enemy in the battle."}},{"n":32,"text":"स संप्रहारस्तुमुलो निशि प्रत्यभवन्महान् ।\nयथा सागरयो राजंश्चन्द्रोदयविवृद्धयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That tumultuous and great clash took place at night like that of two oceans swelled by the rising moon, O king."}},{"n":33,"text":"तत उत्सृज्य पाणिभ्यः प्रदीपांस्तव वाहिनी ।\nयुयुधे पाण्डवैः सार्धमुन्मत्तवदहःक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your army, throwing the torches from their hands, fought the Pandavas like madmen at the day's end."}},{"n":34,"text":"रजसा तमसा चैव संवृते भृशदारुणे ।\nकेवलं नामगोत्रेण प्रायुध्यन्त जयैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the world covered in dust and darkness, most dreadful, those who sought victory fought by name and clan alone."}},{"n":35,"text":"अश्रूयन्त हि नामानि श्राव्यमाणानि पार्थिवैः ।\nप्रहरद्भिर्महाराज स्वयंवर इवाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"For names were heard, called out by the kings as they struck, great king, as in a bride-choice assembly, in the battle."}},{"n":36,"text":"निःशब्दमासीत्सहसा पुनः शब्दो महानभूत् ।\nक्रुद्धानां युध्यमानानां जयतां जीयतामपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suddenly it would be silent, and then a great noise would arise, of the angry, fighting men, winning and losing."}},{"n":37,"text":"यत्र यत्र स्म दृश्यन्ते प्रदीपाः कुरुसत्तम ।\nतत्र तत्र स्म ते शूरा निपतन्ति पतंगवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever torches were seen, best of Kurus, there those brave men fell like moths."}},{"n":38,"text":"तथा संयुध्यमानानां विगाढाभून्महानिशा ।\nपाण्डवानां च राजेन्द्र कौरवाणां च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, as they fought, the great night deepened for the Pandavas and the Kauravas everywhere, O king of kings."}}]}]}